## Paper2Agent and broader capability growth

[[Designs/AI4Research Capability Growth|Architecture assessment]] connects reusable stage CCs, a composed Paper2Agent factory, admission, and eventual system-wide self-improvement. [[Designs/Paper2Agent Capability Factory|Factory mapping]] supplies source-grounded detail. These are proposed follow-on designs. For efficient reading and freshness checks, use [[Designs/Agent Reading and Freshness]].

**The talk:** [[Designs/Paper2Agent Briefing/presentation/README|eight shown slides, about six minutes]] with workflow, coupling and factory-fit diagrams. The proposed factory has a [[Designs/Capability Capsule Factory Feature|one-page feature definition]] and a [[Designs/Paper2Agent Capability Factory|detailed stage note]].

**Presentation reading route:** [[Designs/Paper2Agent Briefing/1 Decision brief|Paper2Agent decision brief]] → [[Designs/Paper2Agent Briefing/2 Agent architecture|How agents should use CCs]]. Two short files with diagrams; detailed assessment above is optional background.

## Standalone benchmark-runner

[[Resources/Coder Prompts/benchmark-runner|Copy the implementation handoff]]: development tooling in our AI4Research branch of JiuwenSwarm, with isolated branch containers, parallel case queues and remote file exports. Developers or their delegated agents may run it. Runtime results never overwrite user files or alter their projects/live state; humans judge the matrix. The separate-repository interpretation is superseded. M2 VM/factory work remains separate.

## M2 sandbox and capability infrastructure

[[Designs/Lab Capsule and Factory Design Plan|M2 roadmap]] → [[Designs/Spark Shared Services and Storage|Spark resource policy]] → [[Designs/VM Lab Infrastructure Design|VM deployment]], [[Designs/Container Capability Capsule Design|container CCs]] and [[Designs/Per Lab Capability Factory Design|local factories]]. [[Designs/Docker Architecture Review and Feasibility|Feasibility review]] records design corrections and untested dependencies.

Target: the supplied 128 GB unified-memory/2 TB GB10 Spark, central host models/inference and bounded ARM64 CPU labs. These are M2 proposals; no registry, factory, two-VM or Spark resource acceptance is claimed. [[Designs/AI4R Lab and CC Images]] and [[Designs/CC as Universal Component]] retain the idea's lineage.

**Optional immediate Spark deployment:** [[Resources/Coder Prompts/spark-benchmark-setup]] prepares the current containers and bounded host storage. It does not gate [[Resources/Coder Prompts/benchmark-runner]] or require M2 VM/factory work.
